{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788364123,"nonce":"Gcxcf3bZIt9hOlP2dMElwQ6CNZ0=","title":"Nothing re-checks a designation once it is placed, so an area change or a herd that walks away makes it inert in silence","message":"`b7359fa` made `designate` answer honestly AT THE MOMENT OF THE CALL. The other\nhalf of what killed `Marco` is that the answer goes stale and nothing notices.\n\nFrom the playbook lesson, which is the incident itself:\n\n\u003e The herd had migrated from x170–182 to x146–155, z39–52 — outside the allowed\n\u003e area — and a hunter will not step outside his area to reach a valid hunt\n\u003e designation. `Marco` starved to death at tick 3,072,772 with five designated\n\u003e deer standing on the map.\n\n**The designations were reachable when they were made.** Even the shipped fix\nwould have reported `accepted_actionable: 6` and been right. Four in-game days\nlater every one of them was inert, and the only thing that changed was that the\nanimals walked.\n\n\n1. **The TARGET moved.** Hunt above all — herds migrate on their own. Slaughter\n   and tame have the same shape.\n2. **The AREA moved.** `area {op:\"remove\"}` or a `posture {area:…}` rebind can\n   put yesterday's mining face outside today's franchise. Nothing re-evaluates.\n3. **The ROSTER moved.** The colony's only miner dies, is downed long-term, or\n   has Mining switched off. `reach.capable` was 2 when the batch was placed and\n   is 0 now. This is C2 of `RUNS/m1-20260901/next-run.md` — 128 designated\n   `MineableSteel` cells, never mined — and it is the half `b7359fa` could only\n   warn about at call time.\n\nToday the workaround is in the lesson, and it is manual: re-run the same\n`designate` with `dry_run:true` over the same targets and read `reach` back.\nThat works (the reach block is computed on a dry run precisely so it does), but\nit needs the agent to already suspect the problem — which is exactly what run\nm1-20260901 never did.\n\n\n`BillWatch` is the precedent and it is a close one: a 250-tick sampler that\nturns a state nobody was polling into a published, named field with a\nconsecutive-failure count, and `bills.ingredient_search` is where it surfaces.\nThe equivalent here is a watch over `designationManager` that scores standing\ndesignations the way `DesignateReach.Score` scores fresh ones, and surfaces on\n`digest` under the presence-is-the-signal rule — because the digest is the read\nthe play loop makes unconditionally, and `turn.md` can then cite a field rather\nthan a procedure.\n\nNote the cost profile is different from `b7359fa`'s: this runs over\ndesignations STANDING on the map, which is a bounded set the manager already\nindexes per def (`SpawnedDesignationsOfDef`), not over a caller's rect. On\nm1-20260901 that was ~138 Mine designations, not 20,000 cells.\n\n\n1. A watch scores standing designations against the capable roster's effective\n   areas, on a cadence, without the agent asking. It reuses\n   `DesignateReach.Score` rather than opening a second route to the same\n   question.\n2. `digest` carries the result under presence-is-the-signal: absent when\n   everything standing is workable, and when it is not, a per-designation-def\n   count plus enough to act — which area, or `capable: 0`, or \"the target\n   moved\".\n3. The three causes are DIFFERENT WORDS, because they are three different\n   corrections (`area`, `work-priorities`, re-designate elsewhere). Presenting\n   them identically is the failure `d9d6c12` names for bill sleep states.\n4. `checklists/turn.md` §materials-designation-loop cites the digest field, and\n   `playbook/a-designation-outside-the-allowed-area-does-nothing.md`'s\n   \"Retire when\" — which currently names exactly this — is discharged.\n5. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-designation-watch.py` on a bench: designate inside the area,\n   shrink the area out from under it, advance, assert the digest says so and\n   names the area.\n\nFound while implementing `b7359fa` (repair round, session 22), and recorded in\nthat lesson's `Retire when` rather than left as a note.","files":null}]}